1. My strongest recommendation: AI Data Governance Copilot

If you're specifically interested in governance, I think this is potentially your strongest POC.

The idea:

"An AI agent that continuously monitors the CDP and acts as a data governance layer."

Segment already has tracking plans, Protocols and privacy capabilities for enforcing data quality and privacy policies.

Your AI layer would make governance intelligent rather than rule-only.

Example

Suppose your application sends:

{
  "event": "card_application",
  "user_id": "12345",
  "email": "akhil@example.com",
  "income": 2500000,
  "pan": "ABCDE1234F",
  "card_type": "premium"
}

Your AI governance agent sees:

PAN → Sensitive PII
Income → Financial information
Email → PII

It could automatically reason:

POLICY:
PAN cannot be sent to marketing destinations.


ACTION:
Remove PAN.


POLICY:
Income can be used for eligibility,
but cannot be sent to advertising platforms.


ACTION:
Mask income before activation.

And produce:

Governance Decision


Event: card_application


✓ email       → Allowed
✓ card_type   → Allowed
⚠ income      → Restricted
✗ PAN         → BLOCKED


Reason:
PAN is classified as sensitive personal information.


Recommended action:
Remove PAN before downstream activation.

That's a very compelling enterprise CDP demo.

